description:
Suggesting to add "description" as an option to the what argument of drive_reveal

For now, I've achieved it by doing this. 

  drive_reveal_description <- function (file) 
  {
    confirm_dribble(file)
    if (no_file(file)) {
      return(put_column(dribble(), nm = "description", 
                        val = character(), .after = "name"))
    }
    googledrive:::promote(file, "description")
  }

Is there a better way?

As I did for readxl. So stick the file in the package and build an accessor function.

We need plain text, csv, jpg, pdf.

@LucyMcGowan Feel free to propose specimens!

https://github.com/r-lib/gargle/issues/12

@craigcitro can you remind me or point me to something re: why this is to be avoided?

Note to self: consider NOT sending an API key with an OAuth token. I.e. only send API key when explicitly in an un-authorized state and sending no token whatsoever. This now seems like the best plan.

I think this can be solved by changing
``` 
   old_doc <- drive_list(path = path,
                          pattern = paste0("^", name, "$"),
                          verbose = FALSE)
    if (!is.null(old_doc)) {
      id <- old_doc$id[1]
    }
  }
```
to 
```
    old_doc <- drive_list(path = output
                          verbose = FALSE)
    if (!is.null(old_doc)) {
      id <- old_doc$id

    }
  }
```
